[SIZE=5][B]Script your Paper server in YAML[/B][/SIZE]
When something happens, if your conditions are true, run your actions. No Java, no Skript: plain YAML rules that are checked when they load, with the file, the path and a "did you mean?" when something is wrong.[/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B]Requirements[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Paper[/B] 1.21.4 or 26.1.x (or a Paper fork) and [B]Java 21+[/B]. Verified on Paper 1.21.4 and 26.1.2.
[*]Not supported: Spigot/CraftBukkit and Folia (OmniEvents uses Paper's Adventure API).
[*]Optional: Vault, WorldGuard, Citizens, Floodgate/Geyser, ProtocolLib, PlaceholderAPI.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]Getting started[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*]Drop the jar into [FONT=Courier New]plugins/[/FONT] and start the server.
[*]Try the English example pack: [FONT=Courier New]/omni pack enable examples[/FONT] (it ships turned off and changes nothing until you enable it).
[*]Edit a rule in [FONT=Courier New]plugins/OmniEvents/rules/[/FONT] or write your own. The plugin's own messages are in Spanish and can be translated in [FONT=Courier New]messages.yml[/FONT].
[*]Run [FONT=Courier New]/omni reload[/FONT]. No restart. Admin commands are OP-only by default.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]Links[/B][/SIZE]
