[/LIST]

[I]Code and documentation were written with the help of an AI coding assistant (Claude), directed and reviewed by the author and verified with an automated in-game test suite.[/I]

[SPOILER="Image transcription"]
[B]Header.[/B] OmniEvents. When X happens, if Y is true, do Z. Built to replace ConditionalEvents: /omni import brings your config, then you get real expressions, live debugging, tests and Bedrock forms. Paper 1.21.4+. Free, MIT. Plain YAML.

[B]See it in game.[/B] Rules from the English example pack, recorded on a real Paper server.
[LIST]
[*][I]Welcome[/I] (examples:welcome): first join: a broadcast ("Please welcome Ana, it's their first time here!"), a starter kit and 100 coins. Then the title "Welcome!" with "Type /daily for your daily reward".
[*][I]/daily streak[/I] (examples:daily): day 5 of the streak pays 5 × 25 coins ("Daily reward: +125 coins (streak: 5 days, you have 250)"). A second /daily the same day: "You already claimed today. Come back in 24h 0m."
[*][I]WorldGuard regions[/I] (examples:mine_haste, examples:vip_only): entering the mine shows "Mining boost on" and gives Haste. Without permission, the VIP area stays closed: "Only VIP players can enter this area."
[*][I]Citizens NPC[/I] (examples:npc_guide, examples:npc_punch): right click: "[Guide] Hi Ana! Try /daily, /shop and /coins." and 4 bread. Hit it: "Guide says: hey, that hurts!"
[/LIST]

[B]Only in OmniEvents.[/B]
[LIST]
[*]/omni debug: see every condition with the value it read, live: player.level (10) >= 3 → true.
[*]Tests in YAML: each rule carries its own tests:. /omni test runs them without players or side effects.
[*]Real expressions: && || ! ( ), math and lists in conditions; if/else and loops inside actions.
[*]Menus → Bedrock: one menu: is a chest GUI on Java and a native form for Bedrock players (Floodgate).
[*]Packs & templates: pack:rule names, extends with ${params}, versions and migrations.
[*]VS Code: a JSON schema gives autocomplete and errors while you type your rules.
[/LIST]

[B]Your YAML → the game.[/B] The welcome rule (trigger player_join; if first_join, a broadcast, a stone sword, 16 bread and pvar.coins = 100; after 2 seconds, the title) next to the screenshot of what the player sees.

[B]Coming from ConditionalEvents?[/B] /omni import translates your config. On top of that you get, in OmniEvents and not in ConditionalEvents: and / or with parentheses and math in conditions; if / else and loops inside actions; debug that shows the value behind each condition; tests inside your YAML; menus that become Bedrock forms; packs, templates and VS Code autocomplete; variables that expire, stored on blocks and items; all-or-nothing costs (Vault money, items, levels). ConditionalEvents, and not OmniEvents, runs on Spigot and on versions before 1.21.4.

[B]How to start.[/B] 1. Install: drop the jar in plugins/, Paper 1.21.4+, Java 21. 2. Try: /omni pack enable examples. 3. Edit: change a rule in rules/ or write your own. 4. Reload: /omni reload, no restart.
[/SPOILER]
